{Dutch Defense: Leningrad Variation, Matulovic Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. Nf3 g6 2. g3 Bg7 3. d4 f5 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. O-O O-O {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. c4 d6 7. Nc3 Nc6 8. b3 ! e5 {Prophylaxis. The move looks slow, and it takes away every active idea the opponent had.} (8... f4 Rb1 fxg3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. dxe5 dxe5 10. Ba3 Re8 11. e4 Nd4 ?! 12. Re1 Nxe4 13. Nxe4 fxe4 14. Nd2 Bf5 15. Nxe4 a5 16. Nc5 b6 17. Ne4 c5 18. Bb2 Ra7 19. Rc1 h6 20. Nc3 Kh7 21. Nd5 Rf7 22. Bxd4 cxd4 23. Be4 Ref8 24. Rc2 Qd6 25. Qd3 h5 26. h4 Kh8 27. Rce2 Kh7 28. Nc3 Bg4 29. Rc2 Rf3 30. Nb5 Qe6 31. Bxf3 Rxf3 32. Qe4 Qf6 33. Rd2 Bh6 34. Rb2 Bg7 35. Nc7 Qf7 36. Nd5 Qd7 37. Nxb6 Qe6 38. Nd5 Rf7 39. Nf4 Qf6 40. Nd3 Bf5 41. Qe2 e4 42. Rd2 exd3 43. Qf3 Qd8 44. Rxd3 Qf8 45. Rd2 Bc8 46. Qd5 Bb7 47. Qe6 Rc7 48. Qh3 Qf3 49. Rde2 Rf7 50. Rd2 d3 51. Re3 Qf6 52. Rexd3 Be4 53. Re3 Bh6 54. Rxe4 Bxd2 55. Re2 Bb4 56. Qe6 Qf3 57. Qe4 Qf6 58. Kg2 Bc5 59. f4 Rd7 60. Qe6 Qg7 61. Qe5 Qf8 62. f5 Re7 63. Qb2 Rxe2+ 64. Qxe2 Qxf5 65. Qf3 Qc2+ 66. Kh3 Qb2 67. Qf7+ Kh6 68. Qf6 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Qxf6 0-1
